# Line endings: the same bytes on Windows, macOS, Linux and CI.
#
# Git for Windows installs core.autocrlf=true, so without this file a Windows
# checkout rewrites every LF as CRLF while macOS and CI keep LF. Prettier's check
# then fails on Windows alone, dart format writes different bytes per machine and
# byte-for-byte generated-file checks disagree. Text is LF in the repository and
# in every working tree; `npm run eol` converts a checkout made before this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe misreads labels and GOTO targets in a batch file with LF endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

